#
# Note: the journal is volatile (/run/log/journal, tmpfs) — `journalctl -b -1` after the reboot
# reports "no persistent journal", so the previous boot's shutdown sequence is not recoverable.
# Also: reading /dev/ttyACM0 needs `sudo -n stty -F ... raw -echo` first (an echoed byte is a real
# EVENT to the firmware's bench stand-in), and the read itself does not reset the Pico (control).
